                                "example_id": "c2dc85bc-6ad0-4365-af4e-94d24d6cf989",
                                "sense_id": "784d4ed6-db52-3b30-8563-5c40f4f4135d",
                                "text": "The demand for special combs for bobbed hair […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "097cdb36-863e-4276-b706-5e502053f052",
                                "sense_id": "784d4ed6-db52-3b30-8563-5c40f4f4135d",
                                "text": "In a typical example from 1924, the BIZ published a photograph of a young, bobbed woman wearing an oversized bow tie and neat mustache, accompanied by the “horrific news” from a North American fashion guru that “[w]hen one does not permit hair to flourish on the head, it will grow on the face and body. The ladies will grow mustaches.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7871d2e-48c2-42b5-8e75-22f794464e37",
                                "sense_id": "784d4ed6-db52-3b30-8563-5c40f4f4135d",
                                "text": "That morning, as she was rushing past them after the first dive, the silver-bobbed woman had yelled, “We're not going anywhere. See you tonight at 6:45.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
